cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, together with the paper it builds on."
title: "Lipschitz pruning meshing: meshing smooth CSG signed distance fields with Lipschitz pruning"
authors:
  - family-names: Allara
    given-names: Lucas
    affiliation: "Universidad Torcuato Di Tella"
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lucas-Allara/Lipschitz-pruning-meshing"
abstract: >-
  An extension of Lipschitz pruning (Barbier et al., Eurographics 2025) from rendering to meshing:
  a sparse octree whose cells each evaluate only the expression tree pruned for them, dual
  contouring with coarse leaves, marching cubes on the octree leaves, and a dynamic update that
  re-meshes only the region a moving primitive reaches, on the CPU and in Vulkan compute on the GPU.
keywords:
  - signed distance fields
  - constructive solid geometry
  - Lipschitz pruning
  - dual contouring
  - marching cubes
  - octree
  - GPU
  - Vulkan
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Lipschitz Pruning: Hierarchical Simplification of Primitive-Based SDFs"
    authors:
      - family-names: Barbier
        given-names: Wilhem
